Torch 2 compatibility for SPOTERTransformerDecoderLayer (correctness: API compatibility).

Demonstrated failure (run upstream-check, torch 2.11, NGC 26.02):
  torch/nn/modules/transformer.py: seq_len = _get_seq_len(tgt, self.layers[0].self_attn.batch_first)
  AttributeError: 'SPOTERTransformerDecoderLayer' object has no attribute 'self_attn'
torch >= 2 also passes tgt_is_causal / memory_is_causal to every decoder layer.

Fix: keep the inherited self_attn module instead of deleting it, and accept the two new keyword arguments.
The overridden forward() still never calls self_attn, so its parameters receive no gradient and SGD never
updates them; the computation is unchanged. Only the stored parameter count grows.

diff --git a/spoter/spoter_model.py b/spoter/spoter_model.py
